--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Windows build published in the Releases section bundles the following
components. They are not part of the NekoFM source code and remain under
their own licenses.

  Electron
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/electron/electron
    The "LICENSE.electron.txt" and "LICENSES.chromium.html" files shipped
    alongside the executable in the release archive contain the full texts.

  Chromium / ffmpeg (as embedded in Electron)
    Chromium is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License; the ffmpeg build
    embedded in Electron is licensed under LGPL/GPL depending on the build.
    Full texts: see "LICENSES.chromium.html" in the release archive.

  lit-html 3.3.3
    License: BSD 3-Clause
    https://github.com/lit/lit
    Vendored verbatim as "src/renderer/assets/vendor/lit-html.js" (unmodified,
    original license header kept; full text in "lit-html.LICENSE" beside it).
    Loaded as an ES module from the same origin, because the app's CSP forbids
    CDN scripts. Used only by the control console's renderer, for patching
    list DOM instead of rebuilding it.

Apart from the vendored lit-html above, the source repository declares no
runtime third-party dependency: the main process runs on Node.js built-ins
plus Electron.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content and accounts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

NekoFM ships no audio, no lyrics, no cookies and no API credentials.
Every user connects with their own accounts and is responsible for
complying with the terms of service of the platforms they use and with
the copyright rules that apply to the content they play.
